# LLM-first — never hardcode intent

Never suggest or implement hardcode / phrase-list / regex whack-a-mole fixes for visitor intent (soft-no, deferral, uncertainty, slang, “nah”, “nope”, “idk”, etc.).

Prefer:
- Live model meaning (LLM-first intent + compose)
- Reply-judge intent checks
- State contracts: settled / waived / do_not_ask fields must not be re-asked
- Ordering fixes (settle waiver **before** the outgoing reply is locked)

Do not add per-field soft-no tip copies, decline keyword tables, or “if visitor says X then Y” phrase lists when the bug is that a settled field was re-asked or live settled after the reply.
